2 DATE 22 AUG 1916
2 PLAC Gol
2 ADDR
3 STAE Buskerud
3 CTRY Norway
1 OCCU biskop i Bjørgvin bispedømme, Biskop i Bergen
1 TITL Bishop
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Willoch_Erichsen
2 CONT
2 CONT Bishop in Tromso, Norway Bishop in Bergen, Norway 2 daugthers with Christiane. 1 son and 5 daugthers with Helga, younger sister of Christiane
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Willoch Erichsen (born February 15, 1842 in Kristiansand, August 22, 1916 in Gol) was a Norwegian theologian and bishop of the Norwegian Church. He was bishop in Bergen diocese from 1899 to 1916.
2 CONT  Johan Willoch Erichsen was born and raised in Kristiansand. His father, Hans Erichsen, was a theologian and served as the cathedral bells. His father died in 1860, the year after John W. Erichsen had been graduated from Cathedral
2 CONC  School. Erichsen followed in his father's footsteps and studied theology at the Faculty of Theology at the University of Oslo, and so came to belong to the generation of priests who had Gisle Johnson as a teacher. Erichsen took a
2 CONC  theological degree in December 1864.
2 CONT  He worked some years as a teacher before he began his ministry, he was employed at Santa School in Christiania and later by his aunt, Katinka Willoch, girl school in the same city. In 1868 he became a staff chaplain in Eidsvold, 
2 CONC first dean of Nils Vogt and from 1870 at Eilert Sundt. Cooperation between Sundt and Erichsen should not have been the best, and at the end of 1873/74, he left to become Eidsvold staff chaplain at Kristian Vilhelm Koren, who was a
2 CONC  pastor in Bragernes and Dean in Drammen. However, he was not long in Drammen either, in May 1875 he was appointed resident chaplain in Skien by Fredrik Petersen, who had been a new professor of systematic theology. He was in Skie
2 CONC n in 15 years, until in 1890 he was appointed pastor of Gjerpen.
2 CONT  Among the former parish priests in Gjerpen there were several bishops, as Knud Gislesen, Johannes Skaar Nilssøn and Andrew Grim Lund. Erichsen was to follow them in that service. The former minister Jacob Sverdrup had been appoin
2 CONC ted bishop in Bergen after Fredrik Waldemar Hvoslef, but due to illness, he had not acceded to the service. Sverdrup died in 1899, and the 30th September the same year, Erichsen appointed bishop of Bergen.
2 CONT  He had resigned as bishop in the 1st May 1916 because of failing health, and died 22 August of that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Erichsen was in 1869 married Sophie Kristiane Rogstad Boeck, born 17 November 1833. Kristiane died in 1873 and in 1877 he married again, with her younger sister, Helga Marie Boeck Margaret, born 1847. In his first marriage he had 
2 CONC two daughters, in his other five daughters and one son.
