1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inga Marie writes - My mother's grandfather Tarald Wilsgaard was born in 1805 at Holmen, an island where fishermen were stationed.  He grew up and married Kirsten Pedersdtr.  Tarald was a storekeeper, and had his o
2 CONC wn business.  He bought fish from the fishermen, dried and bundled them, and sent them by boat to Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT During a long war, warships were patroling the coast of Norway.  One day he saw a big warship out at sea.  He expected a visit, so he took a barrel in the house, put everything of valve in silvercloths, rolled the barrel behind th
2 CONC e barn, and dug it down deep into the manure pile.
2 CONT
2 CONT He did not know they were watching with binoculars.  So they came ashore, did not hurt anyone, just dug out the barrel and left.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Tarald inherited Kongsnes from his father.  They moved the house and what they had to Torsken.  Their four children, Jens Johan, Else Marie, Dorthea Sofie, and Daniel Severin, were raised at Torsken.
