1 OCCU gårdbruker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inga Marie says - My Grandfather liked us grandchildren we knew, because he always gave us something good to eat when he came from the store.
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember my Grandfather always carried green dried peas in his pockets.  When he come up from the store to the house, the pigeons would come sit on his head and shoulders.  Then he would grab the peas from his pockets, and feed 
2 CONC then from his hands.
2 CONT
2 CONT My Grandpa could read, but he could not do arthmetic on paper.  He sat by the laywer, and figured everything out in his head.  No one ever dared cheat him in any way.  He was a very strict businessman and really prospered.  He was
2 CONC  handsome with a long beard, and always smiling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandpa often built coffins, since the graveyard was so close by, and he used the attic for this particular work.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandpa passed away when I was three.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bygdebok pages 355 and 363.  Jens Johan worked a large farm.  They had four cows, a bull, 16 sheep, one goat, and two pigs.  Jens had a business selling fish, and he was very busy in civic work.  He sat on the Township Board for 2
2 CONC 4 years, and was a spokesman during two periods (mayor).  He was almost a priest.  He was a priest's assistant.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
