1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ROLFSEN, JENS CHRISTIAN, student, født på Vestre Aker i Oslo den 11. desember 1923, av Alf Rolfsen, f. 1895, og Ingrid f. Platou, f. 1893, begge i Oslo. Handelsskole, aspirant ved mekaniske verksted. Var med på å u
2 CONC tgi en illegal avis. Flyktet til Sverige 28. juni 1944. Reiste videre til England og kom inn i Den norske marine. Falt som kadettaspirant 12. desember 1944 da korvetten Tunsberg Castle ble rammet av mine eller torpedo og sank i Bå
2 CONC tsfjord.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Final Fate - 1944:  The crew member mentioned above says that on one of the westbound North Atlantic voyages Tunsberg Castle and Eglantine were ordered to return to Liverpool (not noted in the table above) where they for 2 days l
2 CONC oaded food, clothes, shoes and various other goods. Tunsberg Castle also had equipment for 2 radio stations as deck cargo, and on board were several radio technicians and operators. She then proceeded to Loch Ewe to wait for a con
2 CONC voy for Murmansk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tunsberg Castle and Eglantine both escorted JW 62 which sailed from Loch Ewe on Nov. 29 and arrived the Kola Inlet on Dec. 7 (ref link in table above). After a few days in Murmansk the 2 corvettes, along with 2 minesweepers, were 
2 CONC ordered to proceed to Båtsfjord, a small community at the end of a narrow fjord on the north side of the Varanger peninsula, where there had been no ships since the Germans withdrew, and where a radio station was to be established
2 CONC . Tunsberg Castle also had a small landing force consisting of 1 officer and 10 army soldiers on board. Arnold Hague/Bob Ruegg's "Convoys to Russia" states she was in Convoy RA 62 on Dec. 12-1944 when she struck a mine (Makkaur NW
2 CONC  field, laid by Z 33 on Oct 31-1944 - see also this thread on my Ship Forum). This convoy had departed the Kola Inlet on Dec. 10 - follow the link for more info.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the personal account mentioned above there were 2 explosions with less than 1 minute's interval, resulting in the entire after deck and about 25 meters of the port side being blown away. I've also seen another persona
2 CONC l account which confirms the 2 explosions. The latter story also indicates that just prior to striking the mine they had "plotted a mysterious wreck" to starboard and had ventured out of the passage that had been swept by the mine
2 CONC sweepers, in order to investigate. It had turned dark by then, but in the distance they could see that people at Båtsfjord had lit fires along the beach to guide them in. The author of this story suspects the "wreck" was some sort
2 CONC  of a trap to lure them into the mine field. He adds that after things had calmed down somewhat following the explosions they could see the aft deck standing straight up in the air against the dark background, as if they had backe
2 CONC d into a mountainside, so this detail conflicts with the former story.
2 CONT
2 CONT Due to the powerful outward current a couple of the lifeboats drifted off empty. Some men were able to get into a life-net, an oval cork ring with a strong net in the middle to stand in. There were so many in it that they stood in
2 CONC  water almost up to their necks. Imagine the cold - there were even ice flakes floating around in the water! They sang and they prayed, until finally one of the minesweepers found them and took them on board. Eglantine, meanwhile,
2 CONC  had gone all the way up to Tunsberg Castle, in spite of the danger of mines, and positioned herself so close to the ship that those still remaining on board could get across. The doomed ship stayed afloat long enough for the men 
2 CONC to get off, then sank by the stern (70 43 701N 30 07 800E).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 had been killed (out of about 120); they were Oddvar Bertrand Karlsen, Arthur Peder Nesse, Jens Christian Rolfsen, Arnold Schreuder and Oluf Edvard Thoresen. Several had been severely wounded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of the survivors died in the latter phase of the war, having been distributed on other ships. The loss of Tunsberg Castle also meant that the plan for a landbase at Båtsfjord had to be given up, all the equipment having gone 
2 CONC down with the ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that there's a long message in my Norwegian Guestbook from someone who has researched this incident extensively, and does not believe the official mine theory at all any more. I'm afraid I won't have time to translate this en
2 CONC tire message right now, but briefly what he's saying is that his research has lead him to believe that Tunsberg Castle was sunk intentionally by 2 Russian submarines, in order to prevent the Norwegian forces from establishing a di
2 CONC rect line of communications between Finnmark and the U.K.
